  "summary_en": "The Gamma node reshapes the tonal values of a layer, VDB, or attribute by applying an exponential gamma curve. It is commonly used for tone mapping, such as sRGB-style encoding with a value near 2.2, or for artistic adjustments.",
  "inputs": [
    "source: layer, VDB or attribute to correct",
    "gamma (optional): per-pixel gamma value multiplied with the Gamma parameter, then inverted if Invert is on",
    "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Signature: layer type accepted by the source",
    "Mask: how much of the new value mixes with the original; default 1 uses only the new value",
    "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels the effect applies to",
    "Gamma: correction factor; the default behavior is an encoding gamma that raises values to the inverse of the exponent",
    "Invert: switches between encoding and decoding gamma by inverting the exponent",
    "Treat RGBA as Premultiplied: un-premultiplies RGBA before correction and re-premultiplies afterward"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "With premultiplied RGBA layers, enable Treat RGBA as Premultiplied; leaving it off makes low-coverage areas look unexpectedly dark",
    "The page lists the output as gamma, which may be confusing when wiring downstream"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Gamma corrige la courbe tonale d'une couche par une puissance exponentielle, pour l'encodage ou le décodage des couleurs."
